<title>CHINA: China Agricultural Bank in loan to sugar firm.</title>
<headline>China Agricultural Bank in loan to sugar firm.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agricultural Bank of China has extended a 600 million yuan loan to the Guangxi Sugar Company, the Financial News said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The state-run bank's loan was to be used for the purchase and stocking of 150,000 tonnes of sugar, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>China has ordered sugar companies to buy sugar to boost prices and build up stocks.</p>
<p>Guanxi has been China's number one sugar cane-producing region for four consecutive years, the newspaper said. It refined 2.33 million tonnes of sugar in the 1995/96 refining season, accounting for 37.41 percent of the nationwide total.</p>
<p>($1=8.3 yuan)</p>
<p>-- Beijing newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
